From 1925e3feb7d5d7ee7224284fc2183f94637fa37e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Avis <jonathanavis96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:24:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Add standing-process text-model adapter
 (claude-standing); measure it against per-call

Replaces the per-call `claude -p` spawn with one long-lived stream-json child
(recycle after N requests, timeout+fallback to the per-call adapter, warm()/atexit
lifecycle). Measured end-to-end: the mechanism works correctly (no orphaned
processes, no stalls on recycle, clean fallback) but --input-format stream-json
forces --output-format stream-json, which triggers heavier extended-thinking
responses than the original plain -p text mode -- so on this CLI version it is
slower per TYPE_TEXT call (6.5s) than the per-call adapter (4.8s), not faster.
Full numbers and the rejected --bare/--effort attempts are in SPIKE-NOTES.md.
